# Dependency Trace: Jackson Module Bean → REST Serialization

## Overview

When a developer registers a custom `Module` bean in a Spring Boot application, it flows through three repositories before reaching actual JSON serialization at REST endpoints:

```
Module @Bean
  └─→ JacksonAutoConfiguration (Spring Boot)
        └─→ StandardJackson2ObjectMapperBuilderCustomizer.configureModules()
              └─→ Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.modulesToInstall() (Spring Framework)
                    └─→ Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.configure()
                          └─→ ObjectMapper.registerModules() (jackson-databind)
                                └─→ ObjectMapper.registerModule()
                                      └─→ Module.setupModule(SetupContext)
                                            └─→ [serializers/deserializers wired into SerializerFactory]
  └─→ JacksonObjectMapperConfiguration → ObjectMapper bean
  └─→ JacksonHttpMessageConvertersConfiguration → MappingJackson2HttpMessageConverter(objectMapper)
  └─→ WebMvcAutoConfiguration.configureMessageConverters() → converter added to MVC
        └─→ AbstractJackson2HttpMessageConverter.writeInternal() → ObjectWriter.writeValue()
```

---

## 1. Jackson-Databind: Module Registration API

**Repository:** `github.com/sg-evals/jackson-databind--jackson-databind-2.15.2`

### `Module` (abstract class)

**File:** [`src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/Module.java`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/jackson-databind--jackson-databind-2.15.2/-/blob/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/Module.java?L25-88)

The abstract base class all custom modules must extend. Key contract:

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `getModuleName()` | Human-readable name (required) |
| `version()` | Module version (required) |
| `getTypeId()` | Deduplication key; defaults to `getClass().getName()` |
| `getDependencies()` | Returns dependent modules to register first |
| `setupModule(SetupContext)` | **Core registration callback** — called by `ObjectMapper` to let the module wire in serializers, deserializers, type modifiers, etc. |

`SetupContext` (inner interface of `Module`) exposes:
- `addSerializers(Serializers)` → wires into `_serializerFactory`
- `addDeserializers(Deserializers)` → wires into `_deserializationContext._factory`
- `addBeanSerializerModifier(BeanSerializerModifier)`
- `addBeanDeserializerModifier(BeanDeserializerModifier)`
- `addAbstractTypeResolver(AbstractTypeResolver)`

### `ObjectMapper.registerModule(Module)` — lines 842–1044

**File:** [`src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/ObjectMapper.java`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/jackson-databind--jackson-databind-2.15.2/-/blob/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/ObjectMapper.java?L842-879)

```java
public ObjectMapper registerModule(Module module) {
    // 1. Validate name and version are non-null
    String name = module.getModuleName();    // throws if null
    Version version = module.version();      // throws if null

    // 2. Register dependencies first (recursive)
    for (Module dep : module.getDependencies()) {
        registerModule(dep);
    }

    // 3. Deduplicate by typeId if IGNORE_DUPLICATE_MODULE_REGISTRATIONS is enabled
    if (isEnabled(MapperFeature.IGNORE_DUPLICATE_MODULE_REGISTRATIONS)) {
        Object typeId = module.getTypeId();
        if (typeId != null) {
            if (!_registeredModuleTypes.add(typeId)) {
                return this;  // skip if already registered
            }
        }
    }

    // 4. Call setupModule — module hooks into ObjectMapper internals
    module.setupModule(new Module.SetupContext() { ... });
    return this;
}
```

`SetupContext` is implemented as an anonymous class inside this call, delegating directly to the `ObjectMapper`'s `_serializerFactory` and `_deserializationContext._factory` fields — this is where the module's custom serializers become live. See the [SetupContext implementation at lines 879–1044](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/jackson-databind--jackson-databind-2.15.2/-/blob/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/ObjectMapper.java?L879-1044).

### `ObjectMapper.registerModules(Iterable<? extends Module>)` — lines 1077–1084

Simple loop calling `registerModule()` for each module. This is what Spring Framework's builder ultimately calls.

