## 2. Spring Framework: Builder and Converter

**Repository:** `github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11`

### `Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder`

**File:** [`spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java)

A fluent builder for constructing and configuring `ObjectMapper` instances. Key module-related state fields:

| Field | Set by | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `this.modules` | `modulesToInstall(Module...)` | Explicit module instances to register |
| `this.moduleClasses` | `modulesToInstall(Class<>...)` | Module classes to instantiate then register |
| `this.findWellKnownModules` | `modulesToInstall(...)` sets `true` | Auto-register JSR-310, Joda-Time, Kotlin |
| `this.findModulesViaServiceLoader` | `findModulesViaServiceLoader(true)` | Delegate to `ObjectMapper.findModules()` |

#### [`modulesToInstall(Module... modules)`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java?L583-587) — lines 583–587

```java
public Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder modulesToInstall(Module... modules) {
    this.modules = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(modules));
    this.findWellKnownModules = true;   // still register well-known modules too
    return this;
}
```

This is the path Spring Boot's customizer takes. Note that `findWellKnownModules = true` means JSR-310, Joda-Time, and Kotlin modules are also auto-detected on the classpath — even when user modules are supplied.

#### [`configure(ObjectMapper objectMapper)`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java?L710-793) — lines 710–793

The heart of the builder, called from `build()`:

```java
public void configure(ObjectMapper objectMapper) {
    MultiValueMap<Object, Module> modulesToRegister = new LinkedMultiValueMap<>();

    // Step A: resolve module sources
    if (this.findModulesViaServiceLoader) {
        ObjectMapper.findModules(this.moduleClassLoader)
                    .forEach(m -> registerModule(m, modulesToRegister));
    } else if (this.findWellKnownModules) {
        registerWellKnownModulesIfAvailable(modulesToRegister);  // JSR-310, Joda, Kotlin
    }

    // Step B: add explicitly provided module instances (line 721–723)
    if (this.modules != null) {
        this.modules.forEach(m -> registerModule(m, modulesToRegister));
    }

    // Step C: instantiate and add module classes (line 724–728)
    if (this.moduleClasses != null) {
        for (Class<? extends Module> cls : this.moduleClasses) {
            registerModule(BeanUtils.instantiateClass(cls), modulesToRegister);
        }
    }

    // Step D: flatten and register on the ObjectMapper (line 733)
    objectMapper.registerModules(modules);   // ← calls into jackson-databind

    // ... remaining config: dateFormat, features, mixIns, handlerInstantiator ...
}
```

The private [`registerModule(Module, MultiValueMap)` helper at lines 795–802](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java?L795-802) uses the module's `typeId` as a deduplication key: if two modules share a typeId, `modulesToRegister.set(...)` overwrites the earlier one, effectively keeping only the last.

#### [`build()`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder.java?L691-703) — lines 691–703

```java
public <T extends ObjectMapper> T build() {
    ObjectMapper mapper = (this.factory != null)
        ? new ObjectMapper(this.factory) : new ObjectMapper();
    configure(mapper);
    return (T) mapper;
}
```

### `MappingJackson2HttpMessageConverter`

**File:** [`spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/MappingJackson2HttpMessageConverter.java`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/MappingJackson2HttpMessageConverter.java?L58-73)

