### `AbstractJackson2HttpMessageConverter.writeInternal()`

**File:** [`spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/AbstractJackson2HttpMessageConverter.java`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/sg-evals/spring-framework--v6.0.11/-/blob/spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/converter/json/AbstractJackson2HttpMessageConverter.java?L439-494) — lines 439–494

The serialization entry point called by Spring MVC for every `@ResponseBody` / `@RestController` response:

```java
protected void writeInternal(Object object, Type type, HttpOutputMessage outputMessage) {
    ObjectMapper objectMapper = selectObjectMapper(clazz, contentType);

    try (JsonGenerator generator = objectMapper.getFactory()
                                               .createGenerator(outputStream, encoding)) {
        ObjectWriter objectWriter = objectMapper.writer();
        // ... apply serializationView, filters, javaType ...
        objectWriter.writeValue(generator, value);
        // ↑ triggers all serializers registered by Module.setupModule()
    }
}
```

